"Debit total must always equal credit total",
"Narration is written in brackets after each entry",
"Compound entries save time when multiple accounts affected"
]},

{n:4, title:"Ledger and Trial Balance", summary:"Posting, balancing accounts, trial balance preparation, errors",
concepts:[
"<strong>Ledger:</strong> Principal book containing all accounts (personal, real, nominal)",
"<strong>Posting:</strong> Transferring journal entries to ledger accounts",
"<strong>Balancing:</strong> Difference between debit & credit sides = closing balance",
"<strong>Debit balance:</strong> Debit > Credit — usually assets, expenses, drawings",
"<strong>Credit balance:</strong> Credit > Debit — usually liabilities, income, capital",
"<strong>Trial Balance:</strong> Statement listing debit & credit balances — verifies arithmetic accuracy",
"<strong>Errors NOT disclosed by TB:</strong> Omission, commission, principle, compensating",
"<strong>Errors DISCLOSED by TB:</strong> One-sided errors (affecting only one account)",
"<strong>Suspense A/c:</strong> Temporary account for one-sided errors until rectified"
],
formulas:[
["Closing balance of asset","Opening + Debits − Credits"],
["Closing balance of liability","Opening + Credits − Debits"],
["Balancing figure","Difference between two sides"],
["Total of Trial Balance","Σ Debits = Σ Credits (when correct)"]
],
journal:null,
formats:`LEDGER ACCOUNT FORMAT — "T" SHAPE

Dr.           Cash Account                 Cr.
──────────────────────────────────────────────
Date  Particulars   ₹  | Date  Particulars   ₹
