"Add items that increase Cash Book balance when starting from Cash Book",
"Overdraft balances work in reverse direction",
"Prepare on a specific date — usually month-end"
]},

{n:6, title:"Depreciation, Provisions & Reserves", summary:"Depreciation methods, provisions vs reserves, types of reserves",
concepts:[
"<strong>Depreciation:</strong> Systematic allocation of asset's cost over useful life",
"<strong>Causes:</strong> Wear & tear, passage of time, obsolescence, depletion, accidents",
"<strong>SLM (Straight Line):</strong> Equal amount each year; asset reaches zero",
"<strong>WDV (Written Down Value):</strong> Fixed % on book value; never zero",
"<strong>Provision:</strong> Charge against profit for known liability/expected loss",
"<strong>Reserve:</strong> Appropriation of profit for specific purpose",
"<strong>Types of Reserves:</strong>",
"  • General Reserve — for any future need",
"  • Specific Reserve — for specific purpose",
"  • Capital Reserve — from capital profits",
"  • Secret Reserve — hidden reserve",
"<strong>Provision vs Reserve:</strong> Provision = compulsory charge; Reserve = appropriation"
],
formulas:[
["SLM Depreciation","(Cost − Scrap) ÷ Useful Life"],
["SLM Rate %","(Annual Depreciation ÷ Cost) × 100"],
["WDV Depreciation","Book Value × Rate%"],
["Profit on sale","Sale Price − Book Value"],
["Loss on sale","Book Value − Sale Price"],
["Average Period","(Months remaining after first purchase + Months remaining after last purchase) ÷ 2"],
["Depreciation (mid-year purchase)","Cost × Rate% × (Months used ÷ 12)"]
],
journal:`DEPRECIATION JOURNAL ENTRIES

